### JWT Token Revocation Testing

# Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5234

# 1. First, let's try to sign in to get a valid JWT token
# Using admin credentials from seeded data
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Abc123*",
  "signInSource": 2
}

###

# 2. Test accessing a protected endpoint with the JWT token
# Replace the token below with the actual token from the login response
@jwt_token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

###

# 3. Test the logout endpoint (this will blacklist the token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

###

# 4. Try to access the protected endpoint again with the blacklisted token
# This should return 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

###

# 5. Test accessing any protected endpoint with the blacklisted token
# This should also return 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/branches
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

###

# 6. Test with an invalid token format
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_format

###

# 7. Test accessing a public endpoint (should work without authentication)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

###

# 8. Test accessing Swagger (should work without authentication)
GET {{baseUrl}}/swagger/index.html
